// p86 — `String * Any` (Any known to be Int at runtime) doesn't
// crash the LLVM verifier. Reached by the mutation fuzzer (finding
// c001, seed=1 iter=93) — the mutation flipped `+` to `*` in
// p15_map_missing_typed.quirk, producing `"bug: " * v` where `v`
// came from `Map.get(...)` typed as `Any`.
//
// Pre-fix: the operator-overload dispatch in Codegen.cpp required
// R's static type to match the magic method's declared param
// (`String.__mul(self, n: Int)` needs Int). i8* (Any) didn't fit,
// so `rhsFits` stayed false, no magic dispatch fired, and Codegen
// fell through to `mathGen->generateBinaryOp("*", %String*, i8*)`
// → `mul nsw i8* %v, %String* %4` → LLVM verifier abort.
//
// Fix: accept `i8* (Any)` on the RHS during dispatch selection.
// The existing coercion block below the dispatch already knows
// how to unbox Any into whatever the declared param wants (via
// `quirk_opaque_to_int`), so we just needed to stop bailing out
// before that coercion could run.

v: Any = 42
print("bug: " * v)   // "bug: " repeated 42 times, no crash
